From d3620fb9129743cde11c98f8e47134eb390a543b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xiaoyi <ashi009@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 15:23:35 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] rust: let rustc select the Windows subsystem

The C++ console-subsystem default overrides the Rust crate attribute. Disable the optional linker_subsystem_flag feature so rustc controls both the subsystem and its CRT entry point.

Requires rules_cc to enable linker_subsystem_flag by default without implying it from link actions.

For bazelbuild/rules_rust#4296
---
 rust/private/utils.bzl | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/rust/private/utils.bzl b/rust/private/utils.bzl
index b3f5b84..8610226 100644
--- a/rust/private/utils.bzl
+++ b/rust/private/utils.bzl
@@ -31,6 +31,8 @@ load(
 )
 
 UNSUPPORTED_FEATURES = [
+    # rustc selects the Windows subsystem and its matching CRT entry point.
+    "linker_subsystem_flag",
     "thin_lto",
     "module_maps",
     "use_header_modules",
